<script type="text/javascript">
    // Joyce's figure (X.60's): the side AB of a rational plus a medial area,
    // divided at C, the rational DE, and DF (EDGF) equal to the square on AB
    // applied to DE with breadth DG; inside it DH (EDKH) equal to the square
    // on AC, KL (HKML) equal to the square on CB, the remainder MF, and NO
    // through the midpoint N of MG. "Make the same construction as before"
    // is one slide that builds DH, KL, N and NO.
    // Added, all hidden at rest: a solid twin DE (initiallyHidden) so the
    // rational line strokes before DF is applied; transparent targets AC,
    // CB, DG, DM, MG, DK, KM, MN (;0;0;0); a faceless twin DFh of the
    // random-faced EDGF, which would be raised over DH and KL when lit
    // (#140), reached as {DF|DFh}; faceless targets DL (D,M,L,E) and MF
    // (M,G,F,L). No angle is called right in the text, so no markers.
